<div id="features" class="features">
  <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="capture-title">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2 id="capture-title">One app for your highlights on Mac and iPhone.</h2>
      <p>Safari does the highlighting. The Twine app sets it up and keeps what you save.</p>
      <ul class="checks" role="list">
        <li><span><strong>Highlight in Safari on either device.</strong> Twine opens Safari's extension settings for you. Then press your shortcut on Mac, or tap Twine in Safari's page menu on iPhone.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Every highlight keeps its source.</strong> Open one to see its page, when you added it and its word count. Copy the text, a link or Markdown with the source link, or open it in Safari.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>One library on every device.</strong> Highlights sync through your private iCloud, with no account. On iPhone, open Twine to upload new highlights.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
